From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMyGlass <openmyglass@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] cpufreq: interactive: unregister the input handler only
 if registered

input_register_handler() can fail: it takes input_mutex with
mutex_lock_interruptible(), so a signal to the task that starts the
governor (for example a write to scaling_governor) makes it return
-EINTR. The governor then only warns and carries on, but the last
CPUFREQ_GOV_STOP calls input_unregister_handler() anyway, which does
list_del() on a handler that was never added to the input core's lists.

Remember whether the registration succeeded and unregister only then.
A failed registration still leaves the governor running without the
input boost, as before.

This change is licensed under GPL-2.0-only, like the file it changes.
---
 drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c
index bf53b46..a1f0d08 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq_interactive.c
@@ -121,6 +121,8 @@ struct cpufreq_interactive_inputopen {
 
 static struct cpufreq_interactive_inputopen inputopen;
 static struct workqueue_struct *inputopen_wq;
+/* Set while cpufreq_interactive_input_handler is registered. */
+static bool input_handler_registered;
 
 /*
  * Max additional time to wait in idle, beyond timer_rate, at speeds above
@@ -1217,6 +1219,8 @@ static int cpufreq_governor_interactive(struct cpufreq_policy *policy,
 		if (rc)
 			pr_warn("%s: failed to register input handler\n",
 				__func__);
+		else
+			input_handler_registered = true;
 
 		idle_notifier_register(&cpufreq_interactive_idle_nb);
 		cpufreq_register_notifier(
@@ -1244,7 +1248,11 @@ static int cpufreq_governor_interactive(struct cpufreq_policy *policy,
 		cpufreq_unregister_notifier(
 			&cpufreq_notifier_block, CPUFREQ_TRANSITION_NOTIFIER);
 		idle_notifier_unregister(&cpufreq_interactive_idle_nb);
-		input_unregister_handler(&cpufreq_interactive_input_handler);
+		if (input_handler_registered) {
+			input_unregister_handler(
+				&cpufreq_interactive_input_handler);
+			input_handler_registered = false;
+		}
 		sysfs_remove_group(cpufreq_global_kobject,
 				&interactive_attr_group);
 		mutex_unlock(&gov_lock);
